{
  "title": "83: al-Motaffefeen المطففين",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nوَيْلٌ لِّلْمُطَفِّفِيْنَۙ‏(1)\nWAYLUL LIL-MOTAFFEFEENAL.\nWoe unto the defrauders in measuring!\nالَّذِيْنَ اِذَا اكْتَالُوْا عَلَى النَّاسِ يَسْتَوْفُوْنَۖ‏(2)\nLAZEENA EZAK TAALOO A’LAN NAASE YASTAWFOON.\nWho, when take they by measure from the people, demand it full\nوَاِذَا كَالُوْهُمْ اَوْ وَّزَنُوْهُمْ يُخْسِرُوْنَؕ‏(3)\nWA EZAA KAALOOHUM AW-WAZANOOHUM YUKHSEROON.\nBut when they measure unto them, or (when) they weigh unto them, minish they (i.e. deceive)\nاَلَا يَظُنُّ اُولٰٓئِكَ اَنَّهُمْ مَّبْعُوْثُوْنَۙ‏(4)\nALAA YAZUNNO OOLAAA-EKA ANNAHUM MAB-O’OSOONA.\nWhat! Think they not that they shall be raised\nلِيَوْمٍ عَظِيْمٍۙ‏(5)\nLE-YAWMIN A’ZEEMINY.\nFor a Mighty Day\nيَّوْمَ يَقُوْمُ النَّاسُ لِرَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَؕ‏(6)\nYAWMA YAQOOMUN NAASO LE-RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nOn the day when mankind shall stand before the Lord of the worlds?\nكَلَّاۤ اِنَّ كِتٰبَ الْفُجَّارِ لَفِىْ سِجِّيْنٍؕ‏(7)\nKALLAA INNA KETAABAL FUJJAARE LAFEE SIJJEEEN.\nNay! the record of the wicked hast been preserved in the ‘Sajjin\nوَمَاۤ اَدْرٰٮكَ مَا سِجِّيْنٌؕ‏(8)\nWA MAA ADRAAKA MAA SIJJEEN.\nAnd what will make thee know what ‘Sajjin’ is?\nكِتٰبٌ مَّرْقُوْمٌؕ‏(9)\nKETAABUM MARQOOM.\nIt is a Book Written\nوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَۙ‏(10)\nWAYLUNY YAWMA-EZIL LIL-MOKAZZEBEENAL.\nWoe on that day unto the beliers\nالَّذِيْنَ يُكَذِّبُوْنَ بِيَوْمِ الدِّيْنِؕ‏(11)\nLAZEENA YOKAZZEBOONA BE-YAWMID DEEN.\nThose who belie the Day of Judgment\nوَمَا يُكَذِّبُ بِهٖۤ اِلَّا كُلُّ مُعْتَدٍ اَثِيْمٍۙ‏(12)\nWA MAA YOKAZZEBOKA BEHI ILLAA KULLO MO’TADIN ASEEM.\nAnd belieth it not (any one) save every transgressor, a sinner\nاِذَا تُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِ اٰيٰتُنَا قَالَ اَسَاطِيْرُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَؕ‏(13)\nEZAA TUTLAA A’LAYHE AAYAATONAA QAALA ASAATEERUL AWWALEEN.\nWhen, are recited unto him Our signs, sayeth he: (These are only) the stories of yore!\nكَلَّا‌ بَلْ رَانَ عَلٰى قُلُوْبِهِمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(14)\nKALLAA BAL, RAANA A’LAA QOLOOBEHIM MAA KAANOO YAKSEBOON.\nNay! rather, has rusted their hearts, what they used to do\nكَلَّاۤ اِنَّهُمْ عَنْ رَّبِّهِمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ لَّمَحْجُوْبُوْنَ‌ؕ‏(15)\nKALLAAA INNAHUM A’R RABBEHIM YAWMAEZIL LA-MAHJOOBOON.\nNay! verily that day they shall be shut out away from the mercy of their Lord\nثُمَّ اِنَّهُمْ لَصَالُوا الْجَحِيْمِؕ‏(16)\nSUMMA INNAHUM LA-SAALUL JAHEEM.\nVerily, they shall be committed to the flaming fire\nثُمَّ يُقَالُ هٰذَا الَّذِىْ كُنْتُمْ بِهٖ تُكَذِّبُوْنَؕ‏(17)\nSUMMA YOQAALO HAAZAL LAZEE KUNTUM BEHI TOKAZZEBOON.\nThen shall it be said (unto them): ‘‘This is that which ye belied!\nكَلَّاۤ اِنَّ كِتٰبَ الْاَبْرَارِ لَفِىْ عِلِّيِّيْنَؕ‏(18)\nKALLAAA INNA KETAABAL ABRAARE LAFEE I’LLIYYEEN.\nNay! The record of the righteous shall be in the ‘Illiyun\nوَمَاۤ اَدْرٰٮكَ مَا عِلِّيُّوْنَؕ‏(19)\nWA MAA ADRAAKA MAA I’LLIYYOON.\nAnd what will make thee know what the ‘Illiyun’ is?\nكِتٰبٌ مَّرْقُوْمٌۙ‏(20)\nKETAABUM MARQOOMUN-Y.\n(It is) a book written\nيَّشْهَدُهُ الْمُقَرَّبُوْنَؕ‏(21)\nYASHADOHUL MOQARRABOON.\nSee it those who are the near ones unto God\nاِنَّ الْاَبْرَارَ لَفِىْ نَعِيْمٍۙ‏(22)\nINNAL ABRAARA LAFEE NA-E’EMIN.\nVerily the righteous ones shall be in bounteous bliss\nعَلَى الْاَرَآئِكِ يَنْظُرُوْنَۙ‏(23)\nA’LAL ARAAA-EKE YANZOROONA.\nOn exalted couches will they view (the delightful sights)\nتَعْرِفُ فِىْ وُجُوْهِهِمْ نَضْرَةَ النَّعِيْمِ‌ۚ‏(24)\nTA’REFO FEE WOJOOHEHIM NAZRATAN NA-E’EM.\nThou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!’) wilt recognise in their faces, the (delightful) radiance of the bliss!\nيُسْقَوْنَ مِنْ رَّحِيْقٍ مَّخْتُوْمٍۙ‏(25)\nYUSQAWNA MIR RAHEEQIM MAKHTOOMIN.\nThey shall be provided to quaff of pure drink (which shall be) sealed (to others)\nخِتٰمُهٗ مِسْكٌ ‌ؕ وَفِىْ ذٰلِكَ فَلْيَتَنَافَسِ الْمُتَنَافِسُوْنَ‏(26)\nKHETAAMOHU MISK, WA FEE ZAALEKA FAL-YATANAAFASIL MOTANAAFESOON.\nThe seal (being) of musk; For that may aspire (all) those who (wish to) aspire (for bliss)\nوَ مِزَاجُهٗ مِنْ تَسْنِيْمٍۙ‏(27)\nWA ME-ZAAJOHU MIN TASNEEMIN.\nMixed therewith shall be the water of ‘Tasnim\nعَيْنًا يَّشْرَبُ بِهَا الْمُقَرَّبُوْنَؕ‏(28)\nA’YNANY YASHRABO BEHAL MOQARRABOON.\n(Which is) a spring from which drink the Near Ones\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اَجْرَمُوْا كَانُوْا مِنَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا يَضْحَكُوْنَ ۖ‏(29)\nINNAL LAZEENA AJRAMOO KAANOO MENAL LAZEENA AAMANOO YAZHAKOON.\nAnd verily they who are the guilty ones, used to laugh at those who believe\nوَاِذَا مَرُّوْا بِهِمْ يَتَغَامَزُوْنَ ۖ‏(30)\nWA EZAA MARROO BEHIM YATAGHAAMAZOON.\nAnd when they pass by them, wink they at one another\nوَاِذَا انْقَلَبُوْۤا اِلٰٓى اَهْلِهِمُ انْقَلَبُوْا فَكِهِيْنَ ۖ‏(31)\nWA EZAN QALABOO ELAA AHLEHEMUN QALABOO FAKEHEEN.\nAnd when return they unto their people, return they jesting\nوَاِذَا رَاَوْهُمْ قَالُوْۤا اِنَّ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ لَضَآلُّوْنَۙ‏(32)\nWA EZAA RA-AWHUM QAALOO INNA HAA-OOLAAA-E LA-ZAAAL-LOONA.\nAnd when they see them, say they: ‘‘Verily these are the straying ones\nوَمَاۤ اُرْسِلُوْا عَلَيْهِمْ حٰفِظِيْنَۙ‏(33)\nWA MAA URSELOO A’LAYHIM HAAFEZEEN.\nWhile they are sent not over them to be the watchers\nفَالْيَوْمَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مِنَ الْكُفَّارِ يَضْحَكُوْنَۙ‏(34)\nFAL-YAWMAL LAZEENA AAMANOO MENAL KUFFAARE YAZHAKOONA.\nSo, today, those who believe shall be at the disbelievers laugh\nعَلَى الْاَرَآئِكِۙ يَنْظُرُوْنَؕ‏(35)\nA’LAL ARAAA-EKE, YANZOROON.\nOn couches (exalted they shall be) seeing (the delightful sights)\nهَلْ ثُوِّبَ الْكُفَّارُ مَا كَانُوْا يَفْعَلُوْنَ‏(36)\nHAL SUWWEBAL KUFFAARO MAA KAANOO YAF-A’LOON.\nShall not the disbelievers be (also) recompensed for what they used to do?",
  "merits": "Surah al-Motaffefeen (The Defrauders)\nThis Surah was revealed in Makkah and it has 36 verses. Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that if a person recites this Surah in his obligatory prayers, he will be safe from Hell. He will not even see it, hear it or even come close to it. His accounts for deeds will not be taken.\nIt is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that if this Surah is recited on a treasure, it will remain safe. In fact, reciting it on anything keeps it safe, even from the vermin of the Earth."
}
